From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Stage thread_detach, and name a thread that is exiting.

GTA IV reaches a loaded scene and dies 66 seconds later on a thread that
had just been created:

    00c4:err:service:device_notify_proc failed to open RPC handle, error 1722
    00c4:err:seh:handle_syscall_fault syscall fault 0xc0000005
        at libSceLibcInternal.sprx+0x51ef7, address 453a00af4017
    00c4:err:seh:handle_syscall_fault syscall fault in syscall 0x133c
        (win32u #828), return ip 6ffffff06f9f

win32u #828 is NtUserCallNoParam. A thread whose RPC fails and which then
goes away is one exiting, and the only NtUserCallNoParam codes an exiting
thread uses are NtUserExitingThread and NtUserThreadDetach -- the latter
reaching thread_detach and its six frees. 453a00af4017 is not an address
this process could have allocated.

What the fault report cannot say is which code the call was given: by then
the argument is gone, and the fault is inside Sony's libc, where every
path in Wine ends up eventually. So say it at the call. Both codes run
once per thread, so the cost is nothing, and each stage of thread_detach
is named -- the last line printed is the one that faulted.

⚠ If no line appears, the faulting code was some other NtUserCallNoParam
and the thread-exit reading is wrong. That is worth one build to learn.

⚠ Diagnostic only. win32u does not import the libc allocator (its frees go
to Wine's heap through pw_wine_heap_libc.o), so the provenance fix that
RADV needed is not the explanation here, and nothing is changed until the
stage is known.
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
index d18d866860..73a67c887c 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/sysparams.c
@@ -7565,21 +7565,62 @@ static void thread_detach(void)
 {
     struct user_thread_info *thread_info = get_user_thread_info();
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+/* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC. GTA IV reaches a loaded scene and then dies 66 seconds later
+ * on a thread that had just been created:
+ *
+ *     00c4:err:service:device_notify_proc failed to open RPC handle, error 1722
+ *     00c4:err:seh:handle_syscall_fault syscall fault 0xc0000005
+ *         at libSceLibcInternal.sprx+0x51ef7, address 453a00af4017
+ *     00c4:err:seh:handle_syscall_fault syscall fault in syscall 0x133c
+ *         (win32u #828), return ip 6ffffff06f9f
+ *
+ * win32u #828 is NtUserCallNoParam, and a thread that fails its RPC and goes
+ * away is one exiting -- which reaches this function and its six frees. The
+ * faulting address is not a pointer this process could have allocated.
+ *
+ * What the report cannot say is which code NtUserCallNoParam was given: by the
+ * time the handler runs the argument is long gone, and the fault is inside
+ * Sony's libc, where every path in Wine ends up eventually. So say it here.
+ * This runs once per thread, which costs nothing, and each stage below is
+ * named so the last line printed is the one that faulted.
+ *
+ * ⚠ If no line appears at all, the faulting call was some other
+ * NtUserCallNoParam code and the thread-exit reading is wrong -- which is
+ * worth knowing for the price of one build. */
+#define PW_DETACH_STAGE(what) ERR( "pw-detach: %s\n", (what) )
+#else
+#define PW_DETACH_STAGE(what) do { } while (0)
+#endif
+
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "entered" );
     destroy_thread_windows();
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "windows destroyed" );
     destroy_thread_pointers();
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "pointers destroyed" );
     user_driver->pThreadDetach();
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "driver detached" );
 
     free( thread_info->rawinput );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "rawinput freed" );
 
     cleanup_imm_thread();
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "imm cleaned" );
     cleanup_opengl_thread();
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "opengl cleaned" );
     NtClose( thread_info->server_queue );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "queue closed" );
     if (thread_info->idle_event) NtClose( thread_info->idle_event );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "idle event closed" );
     free( thread_info->session_data );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "session data freed" );
     free( thread_info->mouse_tracking_info );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "mouse tracking freed" );
     free( thread_info );
+    PW_DETACH_STAGE( "thread info freed" );
 
     exiting_thread_id = 0;
+#undef PW_DETACH_STAGE
 }
 
 static BOOL set_keyboard_auto_repeat( BOOL enable )
@@ -7622,6 +7663,10 @@ ULONG_PTR WINAPI NtUserCallNoParam( ULONG code )
 
     /* temporary exports */
     case NtUserExitingThread:
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+        /* ⚠ DIAGNOSTIC, see thread_detach. Once per thread. */
+        ERR( "pw-detach: exiting thread\n" );
+#endif
         exiting_thread_id = GetCurrentThreadId();
         return 0;
 
